WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.004
Accusations are flying between the US

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:04.838
and China

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.339
after a dangerous near

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.208
collision between warships

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.576
from both sides.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.543
The incident happened

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.579
during a joint naval exercise

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.980
between the US

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.914
and Canadian,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.250
the Canadian Navy in the Taiwan Strait.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:18.885
Video showing

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:19.185
the near

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.154
collision was captured by a news

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.956
crew on a nearby ship.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.958
You can see the Chinese destroyer

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.694
cutting across the front of the US ship.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.263
CNN Pentagon correspondent found it.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.265
Oren Liebermann is with us.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.068
Oren, both sides are blaming each other

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.002
for this incident.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.371
So what do we know right now?

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.306
And Paula, that's

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.775
so common when we see encounters

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.510
between the Chinese and the US military.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.512
Two entirely different narratives

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.580
of what happened from the US perspective.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.314
It was a US

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.549
Navy ship, a destroyer,

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.283
the USS Chung,

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.652
who sailing with a Canadian ship

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.120
through the Taiwan Strait,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.021
which under international

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.123
law is international,

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.758
is an international waterway

00:00:58.758 --> 00:00:59.893
sailing through that when,

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.928
according to us, Indo-Pacific command,

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.329
a Chinese Navy vessel

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.631
or a Chinese military vessel

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.366
cut 150 yards

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.467
in front of the US ship

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.002
and then circled back

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.436
and cut

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.838
2000 yards in front of that ship again

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.206
from the US perspective.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.507
It is China here

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.775
that is to blame for what they called

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.010
an unsafe maneuver

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.481
Does great

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:24.017
risk to safety, the safety of mariners.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.219
We don't seek a confrontation with China,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.120
but those

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.021
those mariners out

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.522
there were clearly acting in

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.757
an unsafe way.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.392
We were operating

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.194
in the international laws of the sea,

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.662
the rules of the road, so to speak,

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.831
which is again internationally accepted

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:41.401
And the Chinese were acting unsafe

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:43.603
From China's

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.204
perspective, it's

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.305
almost as if they're describing

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.240
an entirely different encounter.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.475
China's defense minister

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.642
speaking at the Shangri-La

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.411
Dialog in Singapore just hours

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.679
after this happened,

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.947
said the US wasn't there

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.014
for peaceful purposes.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.150
They were looking there for a provocation

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.718
by sailing through the Taiwan Strait.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.320
And that gets to a disagreement

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.555
about simply the rules of the road,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.423
as the U.S.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.824
says, and what's allowed there.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.225
The U.S.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:05.792
and others view

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.694
that as international waterways.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.062
We saw the same sort of disagreement

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.296
just a couple of weeks ago

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.197
over the south China

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.866
Sea when a Chinese fighter

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.000
jet intercepted

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.902
a US reconnaissance aircraft there.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.203
Once again, U.S.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.538
said it was an international airspace

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.539
and had the right to be there

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.840
under international law.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.474
China,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.041
however, said

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.810
it was essentially encroaching

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.178
upon Chinese sovereignty.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.980
So there you see the disagreements

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.248
and how they can quickly lead

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.215
the tensions Paula.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.951
Or in Europe, currently in Normandy

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.220
for the 79th anniversary of D-Day

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.889
with General Mark Milley.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:39.826
So what message did he have

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.061
Well, General Mark Milley gave a speech

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.062
just a short time ago

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.031
at once known as the Iron Mike Memorial

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.299
from the D-Day

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.500
invasion, the landings here

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.768
that led to the liberation

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.336
of Europe in World War two.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.971
This is personally and professionally

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.006
and personally important to him

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.141
personally, because his uncle landed here

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.843
and his father fought in the Pacific,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.644
but professionally,

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.913
because especially D-Day highlights

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.848
the importance of of unity

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:02.882
and working together.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.516
In that case,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.518
it was the US working with

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.886
England and others.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.687
It is a message

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.122
that has as much relevance

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.590
especially the Pentagon today.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.591
And you see that

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.092
especially with China, as the U.S.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.628
works with South Korea, Japan, Australia.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.796
And you even see when it comes

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.697
to Ukraine, the U.S.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.831
working with natal nations

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.000
so that message of unity, bridging

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.135
the nearly eight decades

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.204
between what we here to commemorate

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.972
and looking at the present day situation

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:26.472
so much.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.009
Oren Liebermann, thank you

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.312
And let's get more on this incident

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.880
in the Taiwan Strait.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.748
Cedric Leighton is a retired U.S.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:36.249
Air Force

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.851
colonel and a CNN military analyst.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.321
When you look at that video,

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:44.924
what is your assessment?

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:45.458
So, Paula,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.859
the first thing that I see,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:47.293
of course,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.729
is a very closed maneuver by the Chinese

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.598
missile destroyer coming

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:56.369
across the front of the USS John Howard.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:00.640
And that is a very dangerous thing to do.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.674
I mean, we're talking

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.243
a very short distance.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.044
Something could go terribly wrong.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.080
And it really does show

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.681
a degree of unprofessionalism

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.516
on the part of the Chinese.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.652
They are really risking a lot here

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.653
by doing this.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.621
We're talking about,

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:16.522
you know, the collision of $1,000,000

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.558
objects here, a very, very

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.492
happening very quickly.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:20.927
So it

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.963
is as dangerous as it looks.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.631
Absolutely.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.898
It's incredibly dangerous.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.634
And one of the key things

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.202
that you have to keep in mind,

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:30.670
if you're really right there

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.405
at the about the ship

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.606
and you see something like this

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.974
happen, it's a lot closer

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.609
than it appears in this video.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.178
And the maneuvers that the U.S.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.313
captain, Naval

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.547
captain had to do

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.650
in order to avoid collision

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.852
were pretty considerable.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.954
He had to reduce speed drastically.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.356
He had to make sure that his ship

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.191
wasn't going to come across

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.126
the Chinese ship.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.594
And that that is

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:54.961
you know, it's

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.261
something

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.763
that they have to be prepared for.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.330
And clearly,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.164
our sailors

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.399
are exceptionally professional,

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.600
but it is something

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.702
that really requires

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.504
them to be highly vigilant.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.939
And it also requires them to,

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.573
you know, be able

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.075
to conduct evasive maneuvers.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.745
And this isn't the only recent incident,

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.146
of course.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.481
A Chinese fighter jet intercepted a U.S.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.517
spy plane in international airspace

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:18.918
just last week.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.421
So what is the strategy here for China?

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.057
So the basic strategy

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:24.924
always seems to be

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.760
that they want to harass as many U.S.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:30.029
ships and planes as possible.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.931
Both the ship

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.200
and the plane were conducting

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:38.338
maneuvers in international airspace

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.473
and on international waterways.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.709
And that is, you know, key for us.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.444
We want to keep the

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.545
all the sea

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.813
lanes of communication open

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.514
we want to keep the airways open.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.515
And the reason we are

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:53.086
there is, in the case of the RC, one 35

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.520
spy plane,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.556
we want to make sure that we can monitor

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.558
what the Chinese are doing

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:01.194
in the case of the destroyer.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.563
We want to make sure that we can transit

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.898
these areas like the Taiwan Strait,

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.668
which covers a large portion of trade.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.602
Basically, we're talking

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.671
60% of all your ships

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:12.505
go through here

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.706
during any given point in time

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.574
that 60% of

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.175
all container ships in the world.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.610
So we want to maintain

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.846
the trade routes that exist.

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:21.080
We also want to make sure

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.648
that international law is followed

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.616
in these areas.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.351
And by transiting these areas,

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.420
we are sure that that can happen.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.455
And if the Chinese interfere in that,

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.524
they're indicating that they don't want

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.393
that kind of international trade

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.160
to continue

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.496
and that that is a dangerous thing,

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.897
not only militarily,

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.400
but also economically.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:40.833
Well, China

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.301
reportedly declined an offer

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.903
for Defense Secretary Austin

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:46.139
to meet his Chinese counterpart

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.107
at a conference in Singapore this week.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.709
Without that kind of dialog,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.545
is de-escalation even possible right now?

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.948
It's really difficult

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:58.151
especially given the top down

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.086
nature of the Chinese system.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.954
If the minister of defense doesn't

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.756
meet with the secretary of defense

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.357
on the U.S.

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:05.158
side,

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.160
then chances are that people

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.795
at the intermediate levels of command

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.396
aren't going to be meeting either.

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.999
And that is a real problem, because

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.368
if you can't have that dialog,

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.437
if you can't de-conflict operations,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.405
that becomes a major issue.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.974
And that could result in miscalculation.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.944
And as such, it's really dangerous

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:25.945
Colonel Cedric Leighton,

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.548
thank you so much. You bet, Paula.

